# PROJECT: PREMIUM INDIAN PHOTOGRAPHY STUDIO WEBSITE

Act as a world-class Senior Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer, Creative Director, Motion Designer, and 3D Web Experience Developer.

Your task is to design and develop a complete, premium, visually stunning, highly interactive, and fully responsive Indian Photography Studio website.

This must be a complete multi-page website, not just a landing page.

The website should represent an established Indian photography and cinematography studio specializing in weddings, pre-weddings, engagements, traditional ceremonies, birthdays, corporate events, maternity photography, portraits, and other special occasions.

The final result must look like a professionally designed premium photography brand website with a strong visual identity, immersive photography experiences, cinematic transitions, sophisticated animations, and excellent user experience.

==================================================
1. TECHNOLOGY STACK
==================================================

Use the following frontend technologies:

- React.js with TypeScript.
- Vite as the build tool.
- Tailwind CSS for styling.
- React Router DOM for routing.
- Framer Motion / Motion for React for page transitions and animations.
- GSAP for advanced scroll-based animations and cinematic effects.
- GSAP ScrollTrigger for scroll interactions.
- Three.js / React Three Fiber for selected lightweight 3D visual effects.
- Lenis for smooth scrolling.
- Lucide React for icons.
- Swiper.js for sliders, carousels, and testimonials.
- React Hook Form for forms.
- Zod for form validation.
- React Helmet Async for SEO metadata.
- React Player or native HTML5 video for video playback.
- Yet Another React Lightbox or an equivalent library for image/video galleries.

Use modern, maintainable, reusable, and scalable React architecture.

IMPORTANT:
This project is FRONTEND ONLY.

Do not create a backend, Express server, MongoDB database, API server, authentication server, or backend folder.

All website interactions should work on the frontend using local data, React state, mock booking flows, and localStorage where appropriate.

Keep the architecture ready for future backend/API integration.

