16. RESPONSIVE DESIGN
==================================================

The website must work perfectly on:

- Small mobile: 320px–375px.
- Standard mobile: 375px–480px.
- Large mobile: 480px–640px.
- Tablets: 640px–1024px.
- Laptops: 1024px–1440px.
- Desktop: 1440px–1920px.
- Large desktop: 1920px–2560px.
- 4K displays and large-screen TVs.

SPECIAL REQUIREMENT: LARGE TV AND ULTRAWIDE DISPLAY SUPPORT.

Design dedicated responsive behavior for large-screen displays.

On large TVs:

- Use wide cinematic hero layouts.
- Increase image presentation size.
- Use balanced maximum-width content containers.
- Avoid excessively stretched paragraphs.
- Increase typography proportionally.
- Maintain visual balance.
- Support ultrawide image compositions.
- Ensure galleries use more columns where appropriate.
- Preserve appropriate spacing and readability.

Never simply stretch the mobile layout to fit large screens.

Use responsive typography with clamp(), fluid spacing, CSS Grid, and flexible containers.

